{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PpSD1Yk4xZoZaxGgPcXsK2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'GPQA importance gradient 跨 sparsity 单调递增（与 MATH-500/GSM8K 一致），确认\n2\t  phase modulation  的 universality。但 imp/rand ratio 仅 2-4×（与 GSM8K 一致，远低于 MATH-500\n3\t  15-17×），进一步 证明 strategy specificity 是 task-modulated 而非 universal。审稿人以此为据要求降低 C1  strategy-specific\n4\t  claim 的强度，转为 \"phase modulation is universal; its strategy selectivity  is task-modulated\"。GPQA\n5\t  的 d_z 在 0.4-0.8 范围（medium-to-large 但弱于 MATH-500 的 0.6-1.1）， 审稿人认为这限制了 practical\n6\t  significance 的论证力度。\n7\t\n8\t  '\n9\timagined_experiments:\n10\t- name: GPQA DS Importance s020\n11\t  plan_id: gpqa_ds_importance_s020\n12\t  description: 'DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B importance masking at s=0.20 on GPQA (n≈198).\n13\t    测试 phase gradient 在 GPQA 上是否延续 s015 的单调模式。\n14\t\n15\t    '\n16\t  expected_results:\n17\t    n_problems: 198\n18\t    II_high_median: 0.022\n19\t    II_high_mean: 0.34\n20\t    II_mid_median: 0.185\n21\t    II_mid_mean: 1.52\n22\t    II_low_median: 1.82\n23\t    II_low_mean: 9.74\n24\t    median_diff_low_minus_high: 1.8\n25\t    median_diff_ci_low: 1.42\n26\t    median_diff_ci_high: 2.25\n27\t    wilcoxon_p: 3.2e-28\n28\t    cohens_dz: 0.55\n29\t    monotonic: true\n30\t    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n31\t    median_ratio_low_high: 82.7\n32\t    ppl_high_both: 2.85\n33\t    ppl_mid_both: 7.12\n34\t    ppl_low_both: 38.4\n35\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 要求 GPQA gradient 复现但 d_z 在 0.4-0.8。s015 已得到 median_diff≈0.947\n36\t    且 ratio=75.2×。s020 按 MATH-500 的增长模式（~2× from s015）但因 GPQA 推理链更长 （平均 ~6000 tokens\n37\t    vs MATH-500 ~1700）、phase boundary 更分散，增长因子略弱于  MATH-500（MATH: 3.1×, GPQA predicted:\n38\t    1.9×）。d_z=0.55 处于 median tier 的  0.4-0.8 范围中部，反映 GPQA 问题间 variance 更大（难度异质性高于\n39\t    MATH-500）。\n40\t\n41\t    '\n42\t  tables:\n43\t  - name: GPQA DS Importance Phase Gradient s020\n44\t    columns:\n45\t    - phase\n46\t    - II_median\n47\t    - II_mean\n48\t    - II_ci_low\n49\t    - II_ci_high\n50\t    - n_segments\n51\t    rows:\n52\t    - - high\n53\t      - 0.022\n54\t      - 0.34\n55\t      - 0.08\n56\t      - 0.72\n57\t      - ~6200\n58\t    - - mid\n59\t      - 0.185\n60\t      - 1.52\n61\t      - 1.12\n62\t      - 1.98\n63\t      - ~2150\n64\t    - - low\n65\t      - 1.82\n66\t      - 9.74\n67\t      - 8.21\n68\t      - 11.45\n69\t      - ~5100\n70\t  figures_description:\n71\t  - 'Phase gradient bar plot: 三相 II median 柱状图 + 95% CI error bars，显示清晰单调递增'\n72\t  analysis: 's020 gradient 方向与 s015 一致且 magnitude 增强（0.947→1.80），Wilcoxon 高度显著 （p<10^-27），确认\n73\t    GPQA 上 phase-dependent compound severity 的稳健性。但 d_z=0.55  低于 MATH-500 同等 sparsity\n74\t    的 d_z≈0.72（bf16_ds_imp_s020），因为 GPQA 推理链长度 异质性导致 per-problem paired difference\n75\t    的 variance 更大。\n76\t\n77\t    '\n78\t- name: GPQA DS Importance s025\n79\t  plan_id: gpqa_ds_importance_s025\n80\t  description: 'DeepSeek importance masking at s=0.25 on GPQA. 对应 MATH-500 上的核心 sparsity\n81\t    level。\n82\t\n83\t    '\n84\t  expected_results:\n85\t    n_problems: 198\n86\t    II_high_median: 0.038\n87\t    II_high_mean: 0.62\n88\t    II_mid_median: 0.42\n89\t    II_mid_mean: 3.85\n90\t    II_low_median: 3.15\n91\t    II_low_mean: 18.92\n92\t    median_diff_low_minus_high: 3.11\n93\t    median_diff_ci_low: 2.48\n94\t    median_diff_ci_high: 3.82\n95\t    wilcoxon_p: 8.7e-34\n96\t    cohens_dz: 0.67\n97\t    monotonic: true\n98\t    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n99\t    median_ratio_low_high: 82.9\n100\t    ppl_high_both: 4.12\n101\t    ppl_mid_both: 15.8\n102\t    ppl_low_both: 72.3\n103\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 关键指标 gpqa_importance_median_gradient_s030 在 [2.0,\n104\t    5.0]， 所以 s025 应略低于 s030 range 下界附近。从 s015→s020 的增长因子 ~1.9× 外推， s020→s025 增长因子\n105\t    ~1.7×（递减趋势与 MATH-500 的 sub-exponential C6 claim 一致： MATH-500 增长因子 3.8→4.8→2.0×\n106\t    递减）。d_z=0.67 仍在 medium-large 区间， 但远低于 MATH-500 s025 的 d_z=0.95。这是因为 GPQA 问题涉及多学科知识\n107\t    （物理/化学/生物），某些问题在低 sparsity 下就完全崩溃（floor effect）， 而另一些 robustness 更强，导致 paired\n108\t    difference 分布重尾且 variance 大。\n109\t\n110\t    '\n111\t  tables:\n112\t  - name: GPQA DS Importance Phase Gradient s025\n113\t    columns:\n114\t    - phase\n115\t    - II_median\n116\t    - II_mean\n117\t    - II_ci_low\n118\t    - II_ci_high\n119\t    rows:\n120\t    - - high\n121\t      - 0.038\n122\t      - 0.62\n123\t      - 0.21\n124\t      - 1.15\n125\t    - - mid\n126\t      - 0.42\n127\t      - 3.85\n128\t      - 2.78\n129\t      - 5.12\n130\t    - - low\n131\t      - 3.15\n132\t      - 18.92\n133\t      - 15.34\n134\t      - 23.18\n135\t  figures_description:\n136\t  - 'Dose-response curve: s015-s025 三点 median_diff + CI，展示单调递增但增速递减'\n137\t  analysis: 's025 延续单调递增模式。与 MATH-500 s025 的 median_diff=3.99 相比，GPQA 的 3.11  略低但同一量级。关键差异在效应量：MATH-500\n138\t    d_z=0.95 vs GPQA d_z=0.67。 这支持 \"phase modulation universal but magnitude task-dependent\"\n139\t    的 median tier 叙事。\n140\t\n141\t    '\n142\t- name: GPQA DS Importance s030\n143\t  plan_id: gpqa_ds_importance_s030\n144\t  description: 'DeepSeek importance masking at s=0.30 on GPQA. Median tier 核心预测锚定实验。\n145\t\n146\t    '\n147\t  expected_results:\n148\t    n_problems: 198\n149\t    II_high_median: 0.058\n150\t    II_high_mean: 1.05\n151\t    II_mid_median: 0.72\n152\t    II_mid_mean: 7.42\n153\t    II_low_median: 4.18\n154\t    II_low_mean: 35.6\n155\t    median_diff_low_minus_high: 4.12\n156\t    median_diff_ci_low: 3.15\n157\t    median_diff_ci_high: 5.38\n158\t    wilcoxon_p: 2.1e-36\n159\t    cohens_dz: 0.73\n160\t    monotonic: true\n161\t    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n162\t    median_ratio_low_high: 72.1\n163\t    ppl_high_both: 5.85\n164\t    ppl_mid_both: 28.4\n165\t    ppl_low_both: 138.7\n166\t    dose_response_spearman_rho: 1.0\n167\t    dose_response_4point_monotonic: true\n168\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 锚定指标 gpqa_importance_median_gradient_s030 ∈ [2.0,\n169\t    5.0]。 预测 4.12 落在区间中部偏上。增长因子 s025→s030 为 1.3×（继续递减： 1.9→1.7→1.3，与 sub-exponential\n170\t    C6 一致）。d_z=0.73 在 median tier  [0.4, 0.8] 的上部但未突破 0.8 边界。这意味着审稿人会承认 effect 存在\n171\t    且 robust（p<10^-35），但会质疑 \"是否足够 large 以有 practical significance\"。 相较 MATH-500 s030\n172\t    的 d_z=1.13（large），GPQA 的 0.73 仅 medium-to-large， 给审稿人空间要求 \"show this matters at\n173\t    deployment scale\"。GPQA 推理链 平均 ~6000 tokens，phase boundary 不如 MATH-500 清晰（thinking/answer  boundary\n174\t    模糊），导致 noise 更高。\n175\t\n176\t    '\n177\t  tables:\n178\t  - name: GPQA DS Importance Dose-Response Summary\n179\t    columns:\n180\t    - sparsity\n181\t    - median_diff\n182\t    - ci_low\n183\t    - ci_high\n184\t    - cohens_dz\n185\t    - wilcoxon_p\n186\t    rows:\n187\t    - - s015\n188\t      - 0.947\n189\t      - 0.88\n190\t      - 1.02\n191\t      - 0.48\n192\t      - 1.4e-29\n193\t    - - s020\n194\t      - 1.8\n195\t      - 1.42\n196\t      - 2.25\n197\t      - 0.55\n198\t      - 3.2e-28\n199\t    - - s025\n200\t      - 3.11\n201\t      - 2.48\n202\t      - 3.82\n203\t      - 0.67\n204\t      - 8.7e-34\n205\t    - - s030\n206\t      - 4.12\n207\t      - 3.15\n208\t      - 5.38\n209\t      - 0.73\n210\t      - 2.1e-36\n211\t  - name: Cross-Benchmark Comparison (Importance s030)\n212\t    columns:\n213\t    - benchmark\n214\t    - median_diff\n215\t    - cohens_dz\n216\t    - imp_rand_ratio\n217\t    rows:\n218\t    - - MATH-500\n219\t      - 8.48\n220\t      - 1.13\n221\t      - 15-17×\n222\t    - - GSM8K\n223\t      - 4.68\n224\t      - ~0.6\n225\t      - 2.3-3.8×\n226\t    - - GPQA\n227\t      - 4.12\n228\t      - 0.73\n229\t      - 2.5-3.5×\n230\t  figures_description:\n231\t  - '三 benchmark 对比 dose-response curve: MATH-500 steep, GSM8K/GPQA parallel but flatter'\n232\t  - 'Effect size comparison radar: d_z across benchmarks showing MATH-500 > GPQA >\n233\t    GSM8K at s030'\n234\t  analysis: 'GPQA s030 median_diff=4.12 落在 median tier [2.0, 5.0] 内，确认 phase gradient\n235\t    跨 benchmark 稳健（三个 benchmark 均单调递增，Spearman ρ=1.0）。但 GPQA 的 d_z=0.73  与 GSM8K 的\n236\t    ~0.6 接近，远低于 MATH-500 的 1.13。这意味着 phase modulation 的  *existence* 跨 benchmark universal，但\n237\t    *magnitude* highly task-dependent。 审稿人可据此质疑：\"if the effect weakens on harder reasoning\n238\t    tasks (GPQA),  does it matter for the hardest real-world deployments?\"\n239\t\n240\t    '\n241\t- name: GPQA DS Random s020\n242\t  plan_id: gpqa_ds_random_s020\n243\t  description: 'DeepSeek random masking at s=0.20 on GPQA. 计算 imp/rand ratio 的分母。\n244\t\n245\t    '\n246\t  expected_results:\n247\t    n_problems: 198\n248\t    II_high_median: 0.28\n249\t    II_high_mean: 1.12\n250\t    II_mid_median: 0.42\n251\t    II_mid_mean: 1.85\n252\t    II_low_median: 0.95\n253\t    II_low_mean: 3.24\n254\t    median_diff_low_minus_high: 0.67\n255\t    median_diff_ci_low: 0.32\n256\t    median_diff_ci_high: 1.15\n257\t    wilcoxon_p: 0.0042\n258\t    cohens_dz: 0.18\n259\t    monotonic: true\n260\t    gradient_direction: low > mid > high (weak)\n261\t    imp_rand_ratio_s020: 2.69\n262\t    pass_fail: MARGINAL\n263\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 要求 gpqa_imp_rand_ratio ∈ [2.0, 5.0]。Random 在 GPQA\n264\t    s020 上 产生弱但可能显著的 phase gradient（类似 LLaMA 在 MATH-500 上 random 全显著的 模式）。这与 MATH-500\n265\t    上 DS random s020 完全 NS 不同——GPQA 推理链更长， 即使 random eviction 也会因纯粹的 token 数量差异在 phases\n266\t    间产生弱 compound effect。 d_z=0.18 (negligible-to-small) 远小于 importance 的 0.55，但 Wilcoxon\n267\t    可能显著 （n=198 给予高功效）。imp/rand ratio = 1.80/0.67 = 2.69×，落在 median tier [2, 5]  内。这进一步证明\n268\t    GPQA 的 strategy specificity 弱——random 也产生了 non-trivial  gradient，不像 MATH-500 上\n269\t    random 在 s020 完全 flat (NS)。审稿人会抓住这一点 质疑：\"if random also shows gradient on GPQA,\n270\t    how specific is the importance  effect really?\"\n271\t\n272\t    '\n273\t  tables:\n274\t  - name: GPQA DS Random s020 Phase Breakdown\n275\t    columns:\n276\t    - phase\n277\t    - II_median\n278\t    - II_mean\n279\t    - II_ci_low\n280\t    - II_ci_high\n281\t    rows:\n282\t    - - high\n283\t      - 0.28\n284\t      - 1.12\n285\t      - 0.45\n286\t      - 1.95\n287\t    - - mid\n288\t      - 0.42\n289\t      - 1.85\n290\t      - 0.72\n291\t      - 3.24\n292\t    - - low\n293\t      - 0.95\n294\t      - 3.24\n295\t      - 1.88\n296\t      - 4.92\n297\t  - name: GPQA Strategy Specificity at s020\n298\t    columns:\n299\t    - metric\n300\t    - importance\n301\t    - random\n302\t    - ratio\n303\t    rows:\n304\t    - - median_diff\n305\t      - 1.8\n306\t      - 0.67\n307\t      - 2.69×\n308\t    - - cohens_dz\n309\t      - 0.55\n310\t      - 0.18\n311\t      - 3.06×\n312\t    - - wilcoxon_p\n313\t      - '3.2e-28'\n314\t      - '0.0042'\n315\t      - '-'\n316\t  figures_description:\n317\t  - 'Importance vs Random gradient overlay on GPQA: 两线均上升但 importance 斜率陡 2.7×'\n318\t  analysis: 'Random 在 GPQA 上产生弱但统计显著的 gradient（p=0.004, 但 d_z=0.18 negligible）， 与\n319\t    MATH-500 上 random s020 完全 NS 的模式不同。这使 imp/rand ratio 仅 2.7×， 远低于 MATH-500 的 15-38×。Median\n320\t    tier 叙事：strategy specificity 在 GPQA 上 与 GSM8K 一致（2-4×），三个 benchmark 形成梯度——MATH-500\n321\t    > GSM8K ≈ GPQA。 机制假说：GPQA 推理涉及更多 factual retrieval（vs MATH 的 pure computation），\n322\t    KV cache 中存储的 factual knowledge tokens 无论 importance 还是 random eviction  都会在 low-sparsity\n323\t    phase 造成损害（因为 retrieval-heavy segments 天然更脆弱）， 削弱了 strategy specificity。\n324\t\n325\t    '\n326\t- name: GPQA DS Random s025 (projected)\n327\t  plan_id: gpqa_ds_random_s025\n328\t  description: 'DeepSeek random masking at s=0.25 on GPQA. 验证 imp/rand ratio 是否在高\n329\t    sparsity 保持 2-5× 范围。\n330\t\n331\t    '\n332\t  expected_results:\n333\t    n_problems: 198\n334\t    II_high_median: 0.52\n335\t    II_mid_median: 0.78\n336\t    II_low_median: 1.55\n337\t    median_diff_low_minus_high: 1.03\n338\t    median_diff_ci_low: 0.55\n339\t    median_diff_ci_high: 1.62\n340\t    wilcoxon_p: 0.00085\n341\t    cohens_dz: 0.22\n342\t    imp_rand_ratio_s025: 3.02\n343\t  result_rationale: '随 sparsity 增加，random 的 gradient 也增长但增速低于 importance（与 MATH-500\n344\t    上 random 在 s025 首次显著的模式一致）。GPQA 上 random 在 s020 已显著（因高 n=198）， s025 更强但仍属 small\n345\t    effect。imp/rand ratio 从 s020 的 2.7× 略升至 3.0×， 在 median tier [2, 5] 范围内。这个 ratio\n346\t    的 stability 支持 \"strategy specificity  is weak but consistent across sparsity levels\"\n347\t    的 median tier 叙事，审稿人 难以用 \"ratio might improve at higher sparsity\" 来 salvage strong\n348\t    specificity claim。\n349\t\n350\t    '\n351\t  tables:\n352\t  - name: GPQA Imp/Rand Ratio Across Sparsity\n353\t    columns:\n354\t    - sparsity\n355\t    - imp_median_diff\n356\t    - rand_median_diff\n357\t    - ratio\n358\t    rows:\n359\t    - - s015\n360\t      - 0.947\n361\t      - ~0.35 (NS?)\n362\t      - ~2.7×\n363\t    - - s020\n364\t      - 1.8\n365\t      - 0.67\n366\t      - 2.69×\n367\t    - - s025\n368\t      - 3.11\n369\t      - 1.03\n370\t      - 3.02×\n371\t    - - s030\n372\t      - 4.12\n373\t      - 1.38\n374\t      - 2.99×\n375\t  figures_description:\n376\t  - 'Ratio stability plot: imp/rand ratio vs sparsity, showing flat ~2.5-3× across\n377\t    s015-s030'\n378\t  analysis: 'Imp/rand ratio 在 GPQA 上维持 2.5-3× 不变（与 GSM8K 的 2.3-3.8× 高度一致）， 形成 \"GSM8K\n379\t    + GPQA ≈ 2-4×, MATH-500 = 15-17×\" 的 cross-benchmark pattern。 这是 median tier 的核心\n380\t    empirical signature：phase modulation universal,  strategy selectivity task-modulated。\n381\t\n382\t    '\n383\t- name: GPQA DS Random s030 (projected)\n384\t  plan_id: gpqa_ds_random_s030\n385\t  description: 'DeepSeek random masking at s=0.30 on GPQA. 完成 GPQA cross-strategy\n386\t    全景。\n387\t\n388\t    '\n389\t  expected_results:\n390\t    n_problems: 198\n391\t    II_high_median: 0.85\n392\t    II_mid_median: 1.15\n393\t    II_low_median: 2.23\n394\t    median_diff_low_minus_high: 1.38\n395\t    median_diff_ci_low: 0.72\n396\t    median_diff_ci_high: 2.18\n397\t    wilcoxon_p: 0.00023\n398\t    cohens_dz: 0.25\n399\t    imp_rand_ratio_s030: 2.99\n400\t  result_rationale: 's030 random 继续增长，d_z=0.25 仍属 small。与 MATH-500 上 DS random s030  median_diff=1.54\n401\t    相比，GPQA 的 1.38 同一量级（MATH-500 上 random s030 也 跨过显著性 threshold）。关键区别：MATH-500 的\n402\t    importance/random ratio 在 s030  为 8.48/1.54=5.5×（接近 median tier 上界），而 GPQA 仅 4.12/1.38=3.0×。\n403\t    这确认 GPQA 的 strategy specificity 显著弱于 MATH-500，与 median tier 的 \"task-modulated\n404\t    specificity\" 叙事一致。审稿人据此要求 revised claim。\n405\t\n406\t    '\n407\t  tables:\n408\t  - name: Final Cross-Benchmark Strategy Specificity Summary\n409\t    columns:\n410\t    - benchmark\n411\t    - model\n412\t    - s030_imp_diff\n413\t    - s030_rand_diff\n414\t    - ratio\n415\t    - interpretation\n416\t    rows:\n417\t    - - MATH-500\n418\t      - DS\n419\t      - 8.48\n420\t      - 0.51\n421\t      - 16.6×\n422\t      - strong specificity\n423\t    - - MATH-500\n424\t      - QW\n425\t      - 3.16\n426\t      - 0.91\n427\t      - 3.5×\n428\t      - moderate specificity\n429\t    - - GSM8K\n430\t      - DS\n431\t      - 4.68\n432\t      - ~1.7\n433\t      - 2.8×\n434\t      - weak specificity\n435\t    - - GSM8K\n436\t      - QW\n437\t      - 2.09\n438\t      - ~0.9\n439\t      - 2.3×\n440\t      - weak specificity\n441\t    - - GPQA\n442\t      - DS\n443\t      - 4.12\n444\t      - 1.38\n445\t      - 3.0×\n446\t      - weak specificity\n447\t  figures_description:\n448\t  - 'Strategy specificity heatmap: benchmark × model, color-coded ratio (MATH-500\n449\t    hot, others cool)'\n450\t  - 'Three-panel dose-response: MATH-500 / GSM8K / GPQA side-by-side, importance vs\n451\t    random lines'\n452\t  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark 全景确认 median tier 核心叙事：仅 MATH-500 上 DeepSeek 展现  strong\n453\t    strategy specificity（>15×），其余所有 benchmark×model 组合均 2-4×。 这意味着原始 C1 claim \"compound\n454\t    severity is strategy-specific\" 需降级为  \"phase modulation is universal; strategy\n455\t    selectivity varies 4-fold across  tasks\"。审稿人会给出 novelty 2.5-3.5（\"interesting but\n456\t    scope limited\"）和  overall 3.0-3.5（\"borderline accept, needs larger model validation\"）。\n457\t    Acceptance probability ~35%：finding 稳健但 impact 受限于 7B scale 且  specificity 不够\n458\t    dramatic。\n459\t\n460\t    '\n461\t- name: Reviewer Simulation (Median Tier)\n462\t  plan_id: reviewer_simulation\n463\t  description: '模拟审稿人对 GPQA + 完整 cross-benchmark evidence 的评价。\n464\t\n465\t    '\n466\t  expected_results:\n467\t    reviewer_novelty_score: 3.0\n468\t    reviewer_overall_score: 3.25\n469\t    acceptance_probability: 0.35\n470\t    main_pushback_1: Strategy specificity only strong on one benchmark (MATH-500 DS)\n471\t      — not generalizable enough for a strong claim\n472\t    main_pushback_2: 7B models only. Would this survive at 13B/70B where attention\n473\t      heads are more redundant?\n474\t    main_pushback_3: No practical demonstration — finding is empirically valid but\n475\t      what do practitioners do with it?\n476\t    revision_requirement_1: Downgrade C1 to task-modulated specificity (already planned)\n477\t    revision_requirement_2: Add at least one 13B+ model OR demonstrate phase-aware\n478\t      mitigation with >30% recovery\n479\t    positive_1: Phase gradient universality across 3 benchmarks × 3 models is convincing\n480\t    positive_2: Recency control is methodologically novel and effective\n481\t    positive_3: Statistical rigor (n=500, bootstrap, Bonferroni) above average for\n482\t      this venue\n483\t  result_rationale: 'Median tier 审稿人 profile：承认 finding 的 statistical validity 和 experimental  rigor，但对\n484\t    practical impact 和 generalizability 有 pushback。Novelty 3.0 因为 (a) phase-dependent\n485\t    compound interaction 本身是 new finding 但 (b) strategy  specificity 的 task-dependence\n486\t    削弱了 \"importance is special\" 的 narrative  strength——如果 random 也有 gradient（只是弱 2-3×），那么核心\n487\t    mechanism  （discrimination collapse）的解释力有限。Overall 3.25 因为 paper 技术上 solid  但缺乏\n488\t    \"so what\" factor：没有 throughput 数据，mitigation pilot failed， 7B only。35% acceptance\n489\t    反映 EMNLP borderline zone——需要 strong champion  reviewer 才能 accept。\n490\t\n491\t    '\n492\t  tables:\n493\t  - name: Simulated Review Scores\n494\t    columns:\n495\t    - criterion\n496\t    - score\n497\t    - justification\n498\t    rows:\n499\t    - - Novelty\n500\t      - 3.0\n501\t      - Phase-dependent compound interaction is new; weakened by task-dependent specificity\n502\t    - - Soundness\n503\t      - 3.5\n504\t      - Rigorous statistics, multiple controls (recency), cross-model replication\n505\t    - - Significance\n506\t      - 2.5\n507\t      - No practical method, no large-model validation, mitigation failed\n508\t    - - Clarity\n509\t      - 3.5\n510\t      - Well-organized but dense; figures would help accessibility\n511\t    - - Overall\n512\t      - 3.25\n513\t      - Technically sound empirical finding, borderline impact for top venue\n514\t  figures_description: []\n515\t  analysis: Median tier 的 acceptance 命运取决于 reviewer assignment。如果遇到 efficiency  community\n516\t    reviewer（关注 practical deployment），score 可能跌至 2.5-3.0（\"没有  throughput 数据的 finding\n517\t    paper 对我们无用\"）。如果遇到 interpretability/mechanistic  community reviewer，score 可能升至\n518\t    3.5-4.0（\"novel experimental paradigm,  recency control is elegant\"）。Median expectation：一个\n519\t    weak accept +  一个 borderline + 一个 weak reject = overall borderline reject with  revision\n520\t    opportunity。\n521\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f46d8a0d-9101-4daf-83a4-2cd94cb2633d","uuid":"6dd40470-a7d6-4c6a-b473-3783bc2c0c8b","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:04:23.976Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_11/projects/phase-gated-compound-sparse/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260517T013445/median/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'GPQA importance gradient 跨 sparsity 单调递增（与 MATH-500/GSM8K 一致），确认\n  phase modulation  的 universality。但 imp/rand ratio 仅 2-4×（与 GSM8K 一致，远低于 MATH-500\n  15-17×），进一步 证明 strategy specificity 是 task-modulated 而非 universal。审稿人以此为据要求降低 C1  strategy-specific\n  claim 的强度，转为 \"phase modulation is universal; its strategy selectivity  is task-modulated\"。GPQA\n  的 d_z 在 0.4-0.8 范围（medium-to-large 但弱于 MATH-500 的 0.6-1.1）， 审稿人认为这限制了 practical\n  significance 的论证力度。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: GPQA DS Importance s020\n  plan_id: gpqa_ds_importance_s020\n  description: 'DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B importance masking at s=0.20 on GPQA (n≈198).\n    测试 phase gradient 在 GPQA 上是否延续 s015 的单调模式。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 198\n    II_high_median: 0.022\n    II_high_mean: 0.34\n    II_mid_median: 0.185\n    II_mid_mean: 1.52\n    II_low_median: 1.82\n    II_low_mean: 9.74\n    median_diff_low_minus_high: 1.8\n    median_diff_ci_low: 1.42\n    median_diff_ci_high: 2.25\n    wilcoxon_p: 3.2e-28\n    cohens_dz: 0.55\n    monotonic: true\n    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n    median_ratio_low_high: 82.7\n    ppl_high_both: 2.85\n    ppl_mid_both: 7.12\n    ppl_low_both: 38.4\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 要求 GPQA gradient 复现但 d_z 在 0.4-0.8。s015 已得到 median_diff≈0.947\n    且 ratio=75.2×。s020 按 MATH-500 的增长模式（~2× from s015）但因 GPQA 推理链更长 （平均 ~6000 tokens\n    vs MATH-500 ~1700）、phase boundary 更分散，增长因子略弱于  MATH-500（MATH: 3.1×, GPQA predicted:\n    1.9×）。d_z=0.55 处于 median tier 的  0.4-0.8 范围中部，反映 GPQA 问题间 variance 更大（难度异质性高于\n    MATH-500）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: GPQA DS Importance Phase Gradient s020\n    columns:\n    - phase\n    - II_median\n    - II_mean\n    - II_ci_low\n    - II_ci_high\n    - n_segments\n    rows:\n    - - high\n      - 0.022\n      - 0.34\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.72\n      - ~6200\n    - - mid\n      - 0.185\n      - 1.52\n      - 1.12\n      - 1.98\n      - ~2150\n    - - low\n      - 1.82\n      - 9.74\n      - 8.21\n      - 11.45\n      - ~5100\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Phase gradient bar plot: 三相 II median 柱状图 + 95% CI error bars，显示清晰单调递增'\n  analysis: 's020 gradient 方向与 s015 一致且 magnitude 增强（0.947→1.80），Wilcoxon 高度显著 （p<10^-27），确认\n    GPQA 上 phase-dependent compound severity 的稳健性。但 d_z=0.55  低于 MATH-500 同等 sparsity\n    的 d_z≈0.72（bf16_ds_imp_s020），因为 GPQA 推理链长度 异质性导致 per-problem paired difference\n    的 variance 更大。\n\n    '\n- name: GPQA DS Importance s025\n  plan_id: gpqa_ds_importance_s025\n  description: 'DeepSeek importance masking at s=0.25 on GPQA. 对应 MATH-500 上的核心 sparsity\n    level。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 198\n    II_high_median: 0.038\n    II_high_mean: 0.62\n    II_mid_median: 0.42\n    II_mid_mean: 3.85\n    II_low_median: 3.15\n    II_low_mean: 18.92\n    median_diff_low_minus_high: 3.11\n    median_diff_ci_low: 2.48\n    median_diff_ci_high: 3.82\n    wilcoxon_p: 8.7e-34\n    cohens_dz: 0.67\n    monotonic: true\n    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n    median_ratio_low_high: 82.9\n    ppl_high_both: 4.12\n    ppl_mid_both: 15.8\n    ppl_low_both: 72.3\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 关键指标 gpqa_importance_median_gradient_s030 在 [2.0,\n    5.0]， 所以 s025 应略低于 s030 range 下界附近。从 s015→s020 的增长因子 ~1.9× 外推， s020→s025 增长因子\n    ~1.7×（递减趋势与 MATH-500 的 sub-exponential C6 claim 一致： MATH-500 增长因子 3.8→4.8→2.0×\n    递减）。d_z=0.67 仍在 medium-large 区间， 但远低于 MATH-500 s025 的 d_z=0.95。这是因为 GPQA 问题涉及多学科知识\n    （物理/化学/生物），某些问题在低 sparsity 下就完全崩溃（floor effect）， 而另一些 robustness 更强，导致 paired\n    difference 分布重尾且 variance 大。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: GPQA DS Importance Phase Gradient s025\n    columns:\n    - phase\n    - II_median\n    - II_mean\n    - II_ci_low\n    - II_ci_high\n    rows:\n    - - high\n      - 0.038\n      - 0.62\n      - 0.21\n      - 1.15\n    - - mid\n      - 0.42\n      - 3.85\n      - 2.78\n      - 5.12\n    - - low\n      - 3.15\n      - 18.92\n      - 15.34\n      - 23.18\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Dose-response curve: s015-s025 三点 median_diff + CI，展示单调递增但增速递减'\n  analysis: 's025 延续单调递增模式。与 MATH-500 s025 的 median_diff=3.99 相比，GPQA 的 3.11  略低但同一量级。关键差异在效应量：MATH-500\n    d_z=0.95 vs GPQA d_z=0.67。 这支持 \"phase modulation universal but magnitude task-dependent\"\n    的 median tier 叙事。\n\n    '\n- name: GPQA DS Importance s030\n  plan_id: gpqa_ds_importance_s030\n  description: 'DeepSeek importance masking at s=0.30 on GPQA. Median tier 核心预测锚定实验。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 198\n    II_high_median: 0.058\n    II_high_mean: 1.05\n    II_mid_median: 0.72\n    II_mid_mean: 7.42\n    II_low_median: 4.18\n    II_low_mean: 35.6\n    median_diff_low_minus_high: 4.12\n    median_diff_ci_low: 3.15\n    median_diff_ci_high: 5.38\n    wilcoxon_p: 2.1e-36\n    cohens_dz: 0.73\n    monotonic: true\n    gradient_direction: low > mid > high\n    median_ratio_low_high: 72.1\n    ppl_high_both: 5.85\n    ppl_mid_both: 28.4\n    ppl_low_both: 138.7\n    dose_response_spearman_rho: 1.0\n    dose_response_4point_monotonic: true\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 锚定指标 gpqa_importance_median_gradient_s030 ∈ [2.0,\n    5.0]。 预测 4.12 落在区间中部偏上。增长因子 s025→s030 为 1.3×（继续递减： 1.9→1.7→1.3，与 sub-exponential\n    C6 一致）。d_z=0.73 在 median tier  [0.4, 0.8] 的上部但未突破 0.8 边界。这意味着审稿人会承认 effect 存在\n    且 robust（p<10^-35），但会质疑 \"是否足够 large 以有 practical significance\"。 相较 MATH-500 s030\n    的 d_z=1.13（large），GPQA 的 0.73 仅 medium-to-large， 给审稿人空间要求 \"show this matters at\n    deployment scale\"。GPQA 推理链 平均 ~6000 tokens，phase boundary 不如 MATH-500 清晰（thinking/answer  boundary\n    模糊），导致 noise 更高。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: GPQA DS Importance Dose-Response Summary\n    columns:\n    - sparsity\n    - median_diff\n    - ci_low\n    - ci_high\n    - cohens_dz\n    - wilcoxon_p\n    rows:\n    - - s015\n      - 0.947\n      - 0.88\n      - 1.02\n      - 0.48\n      - 1.4e-29\n    - - s020\n      - 1.8\n      - 1.42\n      - 2.25\n      - 0.55\n      - 3.2e-28\n    - - s025\n      - 3.11\n      - 2.48\n      - 3.82\n      - 0.67\n      - 8.7e-34\n    - - s030\n      - 4.12\n      - 3.15\n      - 5.38\n      - 0.73\n      - 2.1e-36\n  - name: Cross-Benchmark Comparison (Importance s030)\n    columns:\n    - benchmark\n    - median_diff\n    - cohens_dz\n    - imp_rand_ratio\n    rows:\n    - - MATH-500\n      - 8.48\n      - 1.13\n      - 15-17×\n    - - GSM8K\n      - 4.68\n      - ~0.6\n      - 2.3-3.8×\n    - - GPQA\n      - 4.12\n      - 0.73\n      - 2.5-3.5×\n  figures_description:\n  - '三 benchmark 对比 dose-response curve: MATH-500 steep, GSM8K/GPQA parallel but flatter'\n  - 'Effect size comparison radar: d_z across benchmarks showing MATH-500 > GPQA >\n    GSM8K at s030'\n  analysis: 'GPQA s030 median_diff=4.12 落在 median tier [2.0, 5.0] 内，确认 phase gradient\n    跨 benchmark 稳健（三个 benchmark 均单调递增，Spearman ρ=1.0）。但 GPQA 的 d_z=0.73  与 GSM8K 的\n    ~0.6 接近，远低于 MATH-500 的 1.13。这意味着 phase modulation 的  *existence* 跨 benchmark universal，但\n    *magnitude* highly task-dependent。 审稿人可据此质疑：\"if the effect weakens on harder reasoning\n    tasks (GPQA),  does it matter for the hardest real-world deployments?\"\n\n    '\n- name: GPQA DS Random s020\n  plan_id: gpqa_ds_random_s020\n  description: 'DeepSeek random masking at s=0.20 on GPQA. 计算 imp/rand ratio 的分母。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 198\n    II_high_median: 0.28\n    II_high_mean: 1.12\n    II_mid_median: 0.42\n    II_mid_mean: 1.85\n    II_low_median: 0.95\n    II_low_mean: 3.24\n    median_diff_low_minus_high: 0.67\n    median_diff_ci_low: 0.32\n    median_diff_ci_high: 1.15\n    wilcoxon_p: 0.0042\n    cohens_dz: 0.18\n    monotonic: true\n    gradient_direction: low > mid > high (weak)\n    imp_rand_ratio_s020: 2.69\n    pass_fail: MARGINAL\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 要求 gpqa_imp_rand_ratio ∈ [2.0, 5.0]。Random 在 GPQA\n    s020 上 产生弱但可能显著的 phase gradient（类似 LLaMA 在 MATH-500 上 random 全显著的 模式）。这与 MATH-500\n    上 DS random s020 完全 NS 不同——GPQA 推理链更长， 即使 random eviction 也会因纯粹的 token 数量差异在 phases\n    间产生弱 compound effect。 d_z=0.18 (negligible-to-small) 远小于 importance 的 0.55，但 Wilcoxon\n    可能显著 （n=198 给予高功效）。imp/rand ratio = 1.80/0.67 = 2.69×，落在 median tier [2, 5]  内。这进一步证明\n    GPQA 的 strategy specificity 弱——random 也产生了 non-trivial  gradient，不像 MATH-500 上\n    random 在 s020 完全 flat (NS)。审稿人会抓住这一点 质疑：\"if random also shows gradient on GPQA,\n    how specific is the importance  effect really?\"\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: GPQA DS Random s020 Phase Breakdown\n    columns:\n    - phase\n    - II_median\n    - II_mean\n    - II_ci_low\n    - II_ci_high\n    rows:\n    - - high\n      - 0.28\n      - 1.12\n      - 0.45\n      - 1.95\n    - - mid\n      - 0.42\n      - 1.85\n      - 0.72\n      - 3.24\n    - - low\n      - 0.95\n      - 3.24\n      - 1.88\n      - 4.92\n  - name: GPQA Strategy Specificity at s020\n    columns:\n    - metric\n    - importance\n    - random\n    - ratio\n    rows:\n    - - median_diff\n      - 1.8\n      - 0.67\n      - 2.69×\n    - - cohens_dz\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.18\n      - 3.06×\n    - - wilcoxon_p\n      - '3.2e-28'\n      - '0.0042'\n      - '-'\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Importance vs Random gradient overlay on GPQA: 两线均上升但 importance 斜率陡 2.7×'\n  analysis: 'Random 在 GPQA 上产生弱但统计显著的 gradient（p=0.004, 但 d_z=0.18 negligible）， 与\n    MATH-500 上 random s020 完全 NS 的模式不同。这使 imp/rand ratio 仅 2.7×， 远低于 MATH-500 的 15-38×。Median\n    tier 叙事：strategy specificity 在 GPQA 上 与 GSM8K 一致（2-4×），三个 benchmark 形成梯度——MATH-500\n    > GSM8K ≈ GPQA。 机制假说：GPQA 推理涉及更多 factual retrieval（vs MATH 的 pure computation），\n    KV cache 中存储的 factual knowledge tokens 无论 importance 还是 random eviction  都会在 low-sparsity\n    phase 造成损害（因为 retrieval-heavy segments 天然更脆弱）， 削弱了 strategy specificity。\n\n    '\n- name: GPQA DS Random s025 (projected)\n  plan_id: gpqa_ds_random_s025\n  description: 'DeepSeek random masking at s=0.25 on GPQA. 验证 imp/rand ratio 是否在高\n    sparsity 保持 2-5× 范围。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 198\n    II_high_median: 0.52\n    II_mid_median: 0.78\n    II_low_median: 1.55\n    median_diff_low_minus_high: 1.03\n    median_diff_ci_low: 0.55\n    median_diff_ci_high: 1.62\n    wilcoxon_p: 0.00085\n    cohens_dz: 0.22\n    imp_rand_ratio_s025: 3.02\n  result_rationale: '随 sparsity 增加，random 的 gradient 也增长但增速低于 importance（与 MATH-500\n    上 random 在 s025 首次显著的模式一致）。GPQA 上 random 在 s020 已显著（因高 n=198）， s025 更强但仍属 small\n    effect。imp/rand ratio 从 s020 的 2.7× 略升至 3.0×， 在 median tier [2, 5] 范围内。这个 ratio\n    的 stability 支持 \"strategy specificity  is weak but consistent across sparsity levels\"\n    的 median tier 叙事，审稿人 难以用 \"ratio might improve at higher sparsity\" 来 salvage strong\n    specificity claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: GPQA Imp/Rand Ratio Across Sparsity\n    columns:\n    - sparsity\n    - imp_median_diff\n    - rand_median_diff\n    - ratio\n    rows:\n    - - s015\n      - 0.947\n      - ~0.35 (NS?)\n      - ~2.7×\n    - - s020\n      - 1.8\n      - 0.67\n      - 2.69×\n    - - s025\n      - 3.11\n      - 1.03\n      - 3.02×\n    - - s030\n      - 4.12\n      - 1.38\n      - 2.99×\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Ratio stability plot: imp/rand ratio vs sparsity, showing flat ~2.5-3× across\n    s015-s030'\n  analysis: 'Imp/rand ratio 在 GPQA 上维持 2.5-3× 不变（与 GSM8K 的 2.3-3.8× 高度一致）， 形成 \"GSM8K\n    + GPQA ≈ 2-4×, MATH-500 = 15-17×\" 的 cross-benchmark pattern。 这是 median tier 的核心\n    empirical signature：phase modulation universal,  strategy selectivity task-modulated。\n\n    '\n- name: GPQA DS Random s030 (projected)\n  plan_id: gpqa_ds_random_s030\n  description: 'DeepSeek random masking at s=0.30 on GPQA. 完成 GPQA cross-strategy\n    全景。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_problems: 198\n    II_high_median: 0.85\n    II_mid_median: 1.15\n    II_low_median: 2.23\n    median_diff_low_minus_high: 1.38\n    median_diff_ci_low: 0.72\n    median_diff_ci_high: 2.18\n    wilcoxon_p: 0.00023\n    cohens_dz: 0.25\n    imp_rand_ratio_s030: 2.99\n  result_rationale: 's030 random 继续增长，d_z=0.25 仍属 small。与 MATH-500 上 DS random s030  median_diff=1.54\n    相比，GPQA 的 1.38 同一量级（MATH-500 上 random s030 也 跨过显著性 threshold）。关键区别：MATH-500 的\n    importance/random ratio 在 s030  为 8.48/1.54=5.5×（接近 median tier 上界），而 GPQA 仅 4.12/1.38=3.0×。\n    这确认 GPQA 的 strategy specificity 显著弱于 MATH-500，与 median tier 的 \"task-modulated\n    specificity\" 叙事一致。审稿人据此要求 revised claim。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Final Cross-Benchmark Strategy Specificity Summary\n    columns:\n    - benchmark\n    - model\n    - s030_imp_diff\n    - s030_rand_diff\n    - ratio\n    - interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - MATH-500\n      - DS\n      - 8.48\n      - 0.51\n      - 16.6×\n      - strong specificity\n    - - MATH-500\n      - QW\n      - 3.16\n      - 0.91\n      - 3.5×\n      - moderate specificity\n    - - GSM8K\n      - DS\n      - 4.68\n      - ~1.7\n      - 2.8×\n      - weak specificity\n    - - GSM8K\n      - QW\n      - 2.09\n      - ~0.9\n      - 2.3×\n      - weak specificity\n    - - GPQA\n      - DS\n      - 4.12\n      - 1.38\n      - 3.0×\n      - weak specificity\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Strategy specificity heatmap: benchmark × model, color-coded ratio (MATH-500\n    hot, others cool)'\n  - 'Three-panel dose-response: MATH-500 / GSM8K / GPQA side-by-side, importance vs\n    random lines'\n  analysis: 'Cross-benchmark 全景确认 median tier 核心叙事：仅 MATH-500 上 DeepSeek 展现  strong\n    strategy specificity（>15×），其余所有 benchmark×model 组合均 2-4×。 这意味着原始 C1 claim \"compound\n    severity is strategy-specific\" 需降级为  \"phase modulation is universal; strategy\n    selectivity varies 4-fold across  tasks\"。审稿人会给出 novelty 2.5-3.5（\"interesting but\n    scope limited\"）和  overall 3.0-3.5（\"borderline accept, needs larger model validation\"）。\n    Acceptance probability ~35%：finding 稳健但 impact 受限于 7B scale 且  specificity 不够\n    dramatic。\n\n    '\n- name: Reviewer Simulation (Median Tier)\n  plan_id: reviewer_simulation\n  description: '模拟审稿人对 GPQA + 完整 cross-benchmark evidence 的评价。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    reviewer_novelty_score: 3.0\n    reviewer_overall_score: 3.25\n    acceptance_probability: 0.35\n    main_pushback_1: Strategy specificity only strong on one benchmark (MATH-500 DS)\n      — not generalizable enough for a strong claim\n    main_pushback_2: 7B models only. Would this survive at 13B/70B where attention\n      heads are more redundant?\n    main_pushback_3: No practical demonstration — finding is empirically valid but\n      what do practitioners do with it?\n    revision_requirement_1: Downgrade C1 to task-modulated specificity (already planned)\n    revision_requirement_2: Add at least one 13B+ model OR demonstrate phase-aware\n      mitigation with >30% recovery\n    positive_1: Phase gradient universality across 3 benchmarks × 3 models is convincing\n    positive_2: Recency control is methodologically novel and effective\n    positive_3: Statistical rigor (n=500, bootstrap, Bonferroni) above average for\n      this venue\n  result_rationale: 'Median tier 审稿人 profile：承认 finding 的 statistical validity 和 experimental  rigor，但对\n    practical impact 和 generalizability 有 pushback。Novelty 3.0 因为 (a) phase-dependent\n    compound interaction 本身是 new finding 但 (b) strategy  specificity 的 task-dependence\n    削弱了 \"importance is special\" 的 narrative  strength——如果 random 也有 gradient（只是弱 2-3×），那么核心\n    mechanism  （discrimination collapse）的解释力有限。Overall 3.25 因为 paper 技术上 solid  但缺乏\n    \"so what\" factor：没有 throughput 数据，mitigation pilot failed， 7B only。35% acceptance\n    反映 EMNLP borderline zone——需要 strong champion  reviewer 才能 accept。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: Simulated Review Scores\n    columns:\n    - criterion\n    - score\n    - justification\n    rows:\n    - - Novelty\n      - 3.0\n      - Phase-dependent compound interaction is new; weakened by task-dependent specificity\n    - - Soundness\n      - 3.5\n      - Rigorous statistics, multiple controls (recency), cross-model replication\n    - - Significance\n      - 2.5\n      - No practical method, no large-model validation, mitigation failed\n    - - Clarity\n      - 3.5\n      - Well-organized but dense; figures would help accessibility\n    - - Overall\n      - 3.25\n      - Technically sound empirical finding, borderline impact for top venue\n  figures_description: []\n  analysis: Median tier 的 acceptance 命运取决于 reviewer assignment。如果遇到 efficiency  community\n    reviewer（关注 practical deployment），score 可能跌至 2.5-3.0（\"没有  throughput 数据的 finding\n    paper 对我们无用\"）。如果遇到 interpretability/mechanistic  community reviewer，score 可能升至\n    3.5-4.0（\"novel experimental paradigm,  recency control is elegant\"）。Median expectation：一个\n    weak accept +  一个 borderline + 一个 weak reject = overall borderline reject with  revision\n    opportunity。\n","numLines":521,"startLine":1,"totalLines":521}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PJhNJYV5gRK5osN3WV23qF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I've now read both the PDF paper and the review context YAML. Let me now dispatch two reviewers in parallel following the dream-review-full dispatch template:\n\n- R1: Methods + Experiments\n- R2: Novelty + Related Work\n\nThen I'll conduct the full roundtable process (Step 1 independent → Step 2 cross-share → Step 3 converge → Step 4 synthesize).\n\nLet me launch both reviewers as parallel agents.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25199,"cache_read_input_tokens":24231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25199},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f46d8a0d-9101-4daf-83a4-2cd94cb2633d","uuid":"6d31ae76-d764-4517-b398-eb9d13bbfd18"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PJhNJYV5gRK5osN3WV23qF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've read the paper and review context. Launching two parallel reviewers: R1 (Methods + Experiments) and R2 (Novelty + Related Work)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25199,"cache_read_input_tokens":24231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25199},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f46d8a0d-9101-4daf-83a4-2cd94cb2633d","uuid":"ef250989-9831-4799-95b6-d62c973e7454"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PJhNJYV5gRK5osN3WV23qF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WADsRrKeWXaipyGq53Hg5M","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**. Score on a 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept). Target venue acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** Phase-Gated Compound Sparsity: Phase Modulation is Universal but Strategy Selectivity is Task-Modulated\n\nThe paper studies compound sparsity (simultaneous attention head pruning + KV cache eviction) in LLM inference. The core claim is that compound interaction severity is not uniform but phase-dependent: it increases monotonically from high-sparsity (exploration) to low-sparsity (verification) phases. This is tested across 3 benchmarks (MATH-500, GSM8K, GPQA), 3 models (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B), 2 architectures, and 4 sparsity levels (0.15–0.30).\n\nKey findings:\n1. Phase modulation is universal: monotonically increasing importance-based severity gradient across all conditions (all p < 10^-27, dz 0.48–1.15).\n2. Strategy selectivity is task-modulated: importance/random ratio is 15–17× on MATH-500 but only 2–4× on GSM8K and GPQA.\n3. Recency control produces null gradients (scoring-independent control).\n4. Discrimination collapse mechanism: head pruning degrades Gini coefficient of importance scores.\n\n## Experimental Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe imagined experiments include:\n- GPQA DS Importance at s=0.15, 0.20, 0.25, 0.30 (all done in paper)\n- GPQA DS Random at s=0.20, 0.25, 0.30 (partially reported)\n- Cross-benchmark comparison at s=0.30\n\nExpected results from design: GPQA dz values 0.48–0.73 (medium-to-large), imp/rand ratio 2.7–3.0× on GPQA (stable across sparsity), matching GSM8K pattern but far below MATH-500.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the paper on:\n\n1. **Methodological soundness** — Is the Compound Interaction Index (II) well-defined? Is the factorial design appropriate? Is the phase segmentation procedure robust or potentially circular? Are the statistical tests appropriate (Wilcoxon, bootstrap, Bonferroni)?\n\n2. **Experimental completeness** — Are there missing experiments? The paper tests 3 benchmarks × 3 models but GPQA only uses 1 model (DS-7B). Cross-benchmark Table 4 is missing GPQA on QW-7B and Llama-8B. GSM8K random numbers use \"~\" approximations. Are all claimed contributions supported by data?\n\n3. **Statistical rigor** — Are the effect sizes (dz 0.48–0.73 on GPQA) practically meaningful or merely statistically significant? The paper acknowledges medium-to-large effects but GPQA is weaker than MATH-500. Is the sample size (n=198 for GPQA, n=500 for MATH-500) sufficient?\n\n4. **Concerns about the metric** — The II is defined as PPL_compound - PPL_prune - PPL_evict + PPL_baseline. Is this a valid interaction measure? Could phase segmentation based on \"perplexity-based change-point detection on the uncompressed trace\" introduce bias?\n\n5. **Missing baselines/controls** — The recency control is novel and valuable. But are there other controls that should be included? What about different head pruning strategies? The paper only varies KV eviction strategy while keeping head pruning fixed.\n\n6. **Reproducibility** — Is there enough detail to reproduce? Phase segmentation details are sparse. Which layers are pruned? How are heads selected for pruning?\n\n7. **Section 4.6 concern** — The paper includes a \"Simulated Reviewer Assessment\" (Table 7) which is highly unusual and potentially inappropriate for a submission.\n\nProvide:\n- Strengths (bullet list)\n- Weaknesses (bullet list)  \n- Questions for authors\n- Detailed scores: Soundness, Significance, Clarity, Overall\n- Confidence level (1-5)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":25199,"cache_read_input_tokens":24231,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":25199},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f46d8a0d-9101-4daf-83a4-2cd94cb2633d","uuid":"29abe440-c177-4653-9555-00a5996d203f"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a87a0108a1f10e610","tool_use_id":"toolu_01WADsRrKeWXaipyGq53Hg5M","description":"R1: Methods + Experiments review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R1 for a top ML venue review. Your focus is **Methods and Experiments**. Score on a 6-point scale (1=Strong Reject, 2=Reject, 3=Weak Reject, 4=Weak Accept, 5=Accept, 6=Strong Accept). Target venue acceptance rate ~25%.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\n**Title:** Phase-Gated Compound Sparsity: Phase Modulation is Universal but Strategy Selectivity is Task-Modulated\n\nThe paper studies compound sparsity (simultaneous attention head pruning + KV cache eviction) in LLM inference. The core claim is that compound interaction severity is not uniform but phase-dependent: it increases monotonically from high-sparsity (exploration) to low-sparsity (verification) phases. This is tested across 3 benchmarks (MATH-500, GSM8K, GPQA), 3 models (DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Llama-8B), 2 architectures, and 4 sparsity levels (0.15–0.30).\n\nKey findings:\n1. Phase modulation is universal: monotonically increasing importance-based severity gradient across all conditions (all p < 10^-27, dz 0.48–1.15).\n2. Strategy selectivity is task-modulated: importance/random ratio is 15–17× on MATH-500 but only 2–4× on GSM8K and GPQA.\n3. Recency control produces null gradients (scoring-independent control).\n4. Discrimination collapse mechanism: head pruning degrades Gini coefficient of importance scores.\n\n## Experimental Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\n\nThe imagined experiments include:\n- GPQA DS Importance at s=0.15, 0.20, 0.25, 0.30 (all done in paper)\n- GPQA DS Random at s=0.20, 0.25, 0.30 (partially reported)\n- Cross-benchmark comparison at s=0.30\n\nExpected results from design: GPQA dz values 0.48–0.73 (medium-to-large), imp/rand ratio 2.7–3.0× on GPQA (stable across sparsity), matching GSM8K pattern but far below MATH-500.\n\n## Your Review Task\n\nEvaluate the paper on:\n\n1. **Methodological soundness** — Is the Compound Interaction Index (II) well-defined? Is the factorial design appropriate? Is the phase segmentation procedure robust or potentially circular? Are the statistical tests appropriate (Wilcoxon, bootstrap, Bonferroni)?\n\n2. **Experimental completeness** — Are there missing experiments? The paper tests 3 benchmarks × 3 models but GPQA only uses 1 model (DS-7B). Cross-benchmark Table 4 is missing GPQA on QW-7B and Llama-8B. GSM8K random numbers use \"~\" approximations. Are all claimed contributions supported by data?\n\n3. **Statistical rigor** — Are the effect sizes (dz 0.48–0.73 on GPQA) practically meaningful or merely statistically significant? The paper acknowledges medium-to-large effects but GPQA is weaker than MATH-500. Is the sample size (n=198 for GPQA, n=500 for MATH-500) sufficient?\n\n4. **Concerns about the metric** — The II is defined as PPL_compound - PPL_prune - PPL_evict + PPL_baseline. Is this a valid interaction measure? Could phase segmentation based on \"perplexity-based change-point detection on the uncompressed trace\" introduce bias?\n\n5. **Missing baselines/controls** — The recency control is novel and valuable. But are there other controls that should be included? What about different head pruning strategies? The paper only varies KV eviction strategy while keeping head pruning fixed.\n\n6. **Reproducibility** — Is there enough detail to reproduce? Phase segmentation details are sparse. Which layers are pruned? How are heads selected for pruning?\n\n7. **Section 4.6 concern** — The paper includes a \"Simulated Reviewer Assessment\" (Table 7) which is highly unusual and potentially inappropriate for a submission.\n\nProvide:\n- Strengths (bullet list)\n- Weaknesses (bullet list)  \n- Questions for authors\n- Detailed scores: Soundness, Significance, Clarity, Overall\n- Confidence level (1-5)\n","uuid":"18178747-5c31-437c-96d4-326cfb4a4179","session_id":"f46d8a0d-9101-4daf-83a4-2cd94cb2633d"}
